{ You have Black and play to win. His king is boxed in the corner, and a knight can never lose a move, so its timing has to be right. }
1. Kh8 { His king steps into the corner: it is his only legal move. } 1... Ne5 { The knight jumps to e5, one hop from g6, the square it mates on. } (1... Ne7 { The knight jumps to e7, also one hop from the mating square. } 2. Kh7 { Also wins, two moves slower: the knight reaches g6 on time by a longer road. [%csl Gg6] }) (1... Nd4 { The knight goes to d4. } 2. h7 Nf5 { Stalemate: a draw. He pushed to h7 when your knight was not one hop from g6, and his king has no legal move. [%csl Rh8] }) (1... Nd8 { The knight heads back through d8. } 2. h7 Ne6 { Stalemate, a draw: his pawn stepped to h7 first, and now his king in the corner cannot move at all. [%csl Rh8] }) (1... Kg6 { Your king goes after his h pawn. } 2. h7 Kf7 { Stalemate: a draw. The pawn escaped to h7 under his king's guard, and when your king came back his king had no move. [%csl Rh8] }) (1... Kf8 { Your king steps to f8, tightening the box. } 2. h7 Ne5 { Stalemate, a draw: after the push to h7 his king is boxed in completely, and your knight move leaves him no move at all. [%csl Rh8] }) (1... Ke7 { Your king steps to e7. } 2. Kg7 Ne5 3. h7 Nf7 4. h8=Q Nxh8 5. Kxh8 { A draw: his king walked out of the corner, and your knight had to give itself for the new queen. Bare kings. [%csl Rh8] }) (1... Kf6 { Your king steps to f6 and lets his king out. } 2. Kg8 Ne5 3. h7 Ng6 4. h8=Q+ Nxh8 { A draw: his king escaped, and your knight could only take his new queen. King and knight alone can never mate. [%csl Gh8] }) 2. Kh7 { His king steps out to h7. } 2... Nd7 { The knight goes to d7, from where it can reach f8 next. } (2... Nd3 { The knight goes to d3. } 3. Kh8 { Also wins, two moves slower: the knight comes back through f4 or e5, still in time. [%csl Gf8] }) (2... Nf3 { The knight hops out to f3. } 3. Kh8 { Also wins, two moves slower: the quickest way back for the knight is through e5, where the dance starts again. [%csl Ge5] }) (2... Nc4 { The knight wanders to c4. } 3. Kh8 { Also wins, but slowly: from c4 the knight has to go back to e5 first, a trip that costs two moves. [%csl Ge5] }) (2... Ng4 { The knight jumps to g4, close to his king. } 3. Kh8 { Also wins, two moves slower: close as it looks, g4 must go back through e5 before the mate. [%csl Ge5] }) (2... Nc6 { The knight goes back to c6, where it started. } 3. Kh8 { Also wins, but the whole trip starts from scratch, two moves later. [%csl Gc6] }) (2... Kf8 { Your king steps to f8. } 3. Kh8 { Also wins, two moves slower: a king step to f8 and back to f7 changes nothing in the knight's timing. [%csl Gf7] }) (2... Kf6 { Your king steps off f7, to f6. } 3. Kg8 { A draw: with your king off f7, his king slips out through g8, and the mating net is gone. [%csl Rg8] }) (2... Ng6 { The knight rushes to g6 at once. Stalemate: a draw. His king on h7 has no square left and is not in check. [%csl Rh7] }) 3. Kh8 { His king steps back into the corner. } 3... Nf8 { The knight lands on f8, one hop from g6. His king cannot step out, so he must push the pawn. } (3... Ne5 { The knight goes back to e5. } 4. Kh7 { Also wins, two moves slower: from e5 the knight must go round to f8 before it can mate. [%csl Gf8] }) (3... Nf6 { The knight jumps to f6, close to his king. } 4. h7 Ne4 { Stalemate, a draw: the pawn reached h7, and from e4 your knight has no mate to give. [%csl Rh8] }) (3... Kf8 { Your king steps back to f8. } 4. h7 Ne5 { Stalemate, a draw: with your king on f8 and his pawn on h7, every square around his king is covered. [%csl Rh8] }) (3... Kg6 { Your king goes for the h pawn. } 4. h7 Nf6 { Stalemate: a draw. Your knight now covers g8, your king covers g7, and his king cannot move. [%cal Gf6g8,Gg6g7][%csl Rh8] }) 4. h7 { His pawn must step to h7, his only legal move. } 4... Ng6# { Mate on g6! Zugzwang forced his pawn onto h7, the last free square beside his king. A knight never loses a move, so its road had to be timed from the start. [%csl Gg6] } (4... Nxh7 { You grab the pawn on h7. A draw: king and knight alone can never mate. [%csl Rh7] }) (4... Ne6 { The knight goes to e6 instead. Stalemate, a draw: his king in the corner has no move and is not in check. [%csl Rh8] }) (4... Nd7 { The knight steps back to d7. Stalemate, a draw: his king has no move, and your knight gave no check. [%csl Rh8] }) (4... Kg6 { Your king goes for the pawn on h7. } 5. Kg8 Nxh7 { A draw: his king slipped out through g8, and a knight alone can never mate. [%csl Rg8] }) 0-1


