{ You have White and play to win. Bishops of opposite colours: yours runs on light squares, his on dark, so they never meet. His bishop can stop one pawn for ever, so you need two, far apart. }
4... Bd8 { His bishop steps to d8 to attack your b pawn. He has nothing better. Push it on to b7. [%cal Yb6b7] } 5. b7 { The pawn reaches b7, a light square his bishop can never touch. Only b8, a dark square, is left for him to guard. } (5. Kc5 { Your king steps to c5 to guard the pawn. } 5... Bg5 { Also wins, about six moves slower: the king guards the pawn instead of pushing it. [%csl Gb6] }) (5. f6 { The f pawn goes first, and leaves the b pawn to his bishop. } 5... Bxb6 6. f7 Ke7 7. f8=Q+ Kxf8 { A draw: his bishop took the b pawn and his king took the new queen. Bishops alone cannot win. [%csl Rf8] }) (5. Ke5 { Your king heads for the f pawn. } 5... Bxb6 { A draw: his bishop takes your b pawn, and one pawn is not enough against his bishop here. [%csl Rb6] }) (5. Bf3 { The bishop steps to f3 and waits. } 5... Bxb6 { A draw: the waiting move lets his bishop take your b pawn, and a lone f pawn cannot beat it. [%csl Rb6] }) 5... Bc7 { His bishop now guards the queening square from c7. Open a second front with the other pawn: to f6. [%cal Yf5f6] } 6. f6 { The f pawn runs for f8, far from the b pawn. His king must watch it, so your king is free to help the b pawn. Now watch. [%tail] } (6. b8=Q { The pawn queens at once, on a square his bishop guards. } 6... Bxb8 7. f6 Bh2 8. f7 Bd6 9. f8=Q Bxf8 { A draw: his bishop took both new queens, on b8 and f8, dark squares it owns. A bishop against a bishop is a draw. [%csl Rb8,Rf8] }) (6. Bf3 { The bishop steps back to f3 for a waiting move. } 6... Ke7 7. b8=Q Bxb8 8. f6+ Kxf6 { A draw: the wasted move let his king reach e7, and now your f pawn falls too. [%csl Rf6] }) 6... Bf4 7. Bf3 Bh2 8. Bg4+ Ke8 9. Ke6 Bg3 10. Bf5 Bh2 11. Bg6+ Kf8 12. Kd7 Bg3 13. Kc8 Kg8 14. b8=Q Bxb8 15. Kxb8 { His bishop gave itself for your b pawn: two pawns far apart beat a bishop of the opposite colour. [%csl Gb8] } 1-0


